-- title:
--   Kernel degree is invariant under a coefficient-ring isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ and $B'$ be commutative rings (in the same universe), let $f : B \to B'$ be a ring homomorphism which is bijective as a function, let $\varphi : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to B[[X_0,X_1]]$ be a pair of formal power series in two variables over $B$ (the type `Series B`), and let $d$ be a natural number. Assume `HasKernelOfDegree` $\varphi\ d$, that is: the kernel algebra $\mathrm{KerAlgebra}\,\varphi = B[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the range of $\varphi$, is a finite $B$-module and a projective $B$-module, and for every field $\kappa$ (in the universe of $B$) and every ring homomorphism $g : B \to \kappa$ the $\kappa$-vector space $\kappa[[X_0,X_1]]/(g\varphi_0, g\varphi_1)$, i.e. $\mathrm{KerAlgebra}$ of the coefficientwise image $\varphi.\mathrm{map}\ g$, has $\mathrm{finrank}$ equal to $d$. The conclusion is that the pair $\varphi.\mathrm{map}\ f$ over $B'$, obtained by applying $f$ to all coefficients, again satisfies `HasKernelOfDegree` with the same $d$: its kernel algebra is finite and projective over $B'$, and all its field-valued fibres have dimension $d$.
--
--   This is the invariance of the property of having a finite locally free kernel of a given degree under an isomorphism of the coefficient ring; the typical application is a reduction map $L \to L/pL$ for a ring with $p = 0$, which is bijective without being an identity of types. It feeds the height and isogeny bookkeeping for formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development, and is cited by the statements producing kernels of degree $4h + 2\,\mathrm{vdet}$, rigidified fake elliptic curves over algebraically closed fields, and quotient bridges realising isogenies of height $4h$.
